  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the OpenSSF Open Source Project Security (OSPS) Baseline at release v2026.08.28: the eight control families (Access Control, Build and Release, Documentation, Governance, Legal, Quality, Security Assessment, Vulnerability Management), every assessment requirement by maturity level 1 to 3, how to scope, evidence and self-attest an assessment of a repository, and the published relates-to mappings to Scorecard, the EU CRA, NIST SSDF, CSF, SP 800-161, SLSA and other frameworks. It also covers OpenSSF Scorecard v5 (pinned at v5.5.0) as a family: the checks, their risk levels and scoring, the aggregate score, maintainer annotations, probes, and running Scorecard in CI with scorecard-action. Version lines: Baseline v2026.08.28 is current, the in-development version is tracked as a preview, and v2026.02.19, v2025.10.10 and v2025.02.25 are legacy; Scorecard v5 is current and Scorecard v4 is legacy. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out the version lines, Level 1 controls, Level 2 and 3 controls, the assessment and mappings, and Scorecard.",
